                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                        "entry_id": "40f977de-f2f3-3b77-b797-e3070be7ea7e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Plante rudérale de la famille des euphorbiacées, aux feuilles opposées disposées par paires en croix, et dont les graines donnent une huile purgative."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3846d59b-7a53-460f-9e35-636cc2e49bbe",
                                "sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                                "text": "Le ricin commun se nomme aussi grande épurge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1030808-d3f3-410b-a04c-34260c7a41e5",
                                "sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                                "text": "La lauréole, ou daphné lauréole se nomme aussi laurier épurge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53ba2697-7ce6-4044-81a8-1e2f1138a6f5",
                                "sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                                "text": "C’est chez Littré et son Dictionnaire de la langue française qu’on déniche une catherinette avec une définition laconique : « Un des noms vulgaire de l’épurge », qui donnait une huile particulièrement purgative et dont le suc était utilisé par les mendiants pour provoquer des plaies artificielles propres a exciter la pitié."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f8428e2a-3cd2-4d17-8751-91bc188e2f28",
                        "source_entry_id": "40f977de-f2f3-3b77-b797-e3070be7ea7e",
                        "source_sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                        "target_lang_word": "kreuzblättrige wolfsmilch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ffb61cd2-d347-435b-8a91-bd517f3dd2a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "40f977de-f2f3-3b77-b797-e3070be7ea7e",
                        "source_sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                        "target_lang_word": "caper spurge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "caper spurge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46d34e19-542f-308f-a31b-c727faefe59c",
                                        "entry_id": "11642791-41c9-3268-a9d7-bacd3d1d431e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An erect, biennial spurge native to southern Europe, northern Africa, and southwest Asia into central Asia, of species Euphorbia lathyris."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "711815d9-99f9-48e5-9ed9-720e4ab32e0d",
                                                "sense_id": "46d34e19-542f-308f-a31b-c727faefe59c",
                                                "text": "The common name, Caper Spurge, alludes to the resemblance of the spongy capsules to capers, which are young flower buds from quite a different plant, Capparis. Caper Spurge fruits were mistakenly pickled by several women and when ingested caused severe illness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82b8b0a8-2e30-4dc0-a0b2-b35672a54419",
                                                "sense_id": "46d34e19-542f-308f-a31b-c727faefe59c",
                                                "text": "\"Sounds delightful,\" Ada said. She looked uneasy. \"Have you ever heard of caper spurge poisoning?\"\n\"Yes, when we go to Mt. Etna, Tazio tells me not to pick the capers with the purple flowers. What do you know about caper spurge?\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af89d0be-ee39-4fec-be0b-a1840933a428",
                        "source_entry_id": "40f977de-f2f3-3b77-b797-e3070be7ea7e",
                        "source_sense_id": "47229fd3-649d-3480-8945-0c28d1818d06",
                        "target_lang_word": "paper spurge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paper spurge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f460633-a4ba-3642-b9c3-ea16e1c416e7",
                                        "entry_id": "e79337b0-08fa-3f1c-9bf7-8643b6b98de8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caper spurge (Euphorbia lathyris)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69876b4b-eeff-4946-a7ce-aa7001dec61c",
                                                "sense_id": "9f460633-a4ba-3642-b9c3-ea16e1c416e7",
                                                "text": "The milky sap (latex) is highly irritating , and can produce serious inflammation of the eyes and skin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac552b04-0988-4257-825b-025b9f370768",
                                                "sense_id": "9f460633-a4ba-3642-b9c3-ea16e1c416e7",
                                                "text": "The oil from the seeds of paper spurge Euphorbia lathyris is now being considered as a raw material for biodiesel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
